## How to test?

- Add / remove / edit things in `files.associations` (`string -> string` pairs)
- Add / remove / edit things in `emmet.variables` (`enum -> string` pairs)

## Supported Settings

All settings that have a [type](https://json-schema.org/draft/2019-09/json-schema-validation.html#rfc.section.6.1.1) `object`, and specify [`properties`](https://json-schema.org/draft/2019-09/json-schema-core.html#rfc.section.9.3.2.1) and/or [`patternProperties`](https://json-schema.org/draft/2019-09/json-schema-core.html#rfc.section.9.3.2.2) such that all JSON schemas within them are of [type](https://json-schema.org/draft/2019-09/json-schema-validation.html#rfc.section.6.1.1) `string`.

### Examples

#### Supported

```json
"extension.variable": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "foo": { "type": "string" },
        "bar": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
                "val1",
                "val2"
            ],
            "enumDescriptions": [
                "Description of 1",
                "Description of 2"
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

```json
"extension.variable": {
    "type": "object",
    "patternProperties": {
        "\\.foo-bar$": { "type": "string" },
        "\\.hello-world$": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
                "val1",
                "val2"
            ],
            "enumDescriptions": [
                "Description of 1",
                "Description of 2"
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

#### Unsupported

```json
"extension.variable": {
    "type": "object",
    "patternProperties": {
        "\\.foo-bar$": { "type": "boolean" },
        "\\.hello-world$": { "type": "string" }
    }
},
```

Boolean types not supported ☝️ 

```json
"extension.variable": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "foo": { "type": "string" }
    },
    "patternProperties": {
        "\\.foo-bar$": { "type": "number" }
    }
},
```

Both `pattern` and `patternProperties` should have `string` type schemas ☝️

This PR fixes #98673

